html+='''<section class="workflow" id="cleanup"><h2>One review before anything moves.</h2><p>This flow belongs in every direction. The action says what will happen, and the result reports what actually changed. Selected size is never a promise of freed space.</p><div class="flowgrid"><div class="reviewcard"><h3>Move Build cache to Trash?</h3><p>Computer › Home › Caches › Build cache</p><p>1 folder · 24 GiB selected</p><p>Files stay recoverable in the system Trash. Disk space usually stays occupied until the Trash is emptied.</p><div class="primary">Move to Trash</div></div><div class="reviewcard"><h3>Permanently remove Build cache?</h3><p>Computer › Home › Caches › Build cache</p><p>1 folder · 24 GiB selected</p><p>This cannot be undone by Blockyard. Shared filesystem blocks or snapshots may keep some space occupied.</p><div class="primary danger">Permanently remove</div></div></div><div class="themerow"><div class="themesample"><h4>Your current theme / Overtaking Landscape</h4><div class="minitiles"><span>Code</span><span>Scratch</span><span>Cache</span></div></div><div class="themesample light"><h4>Light-theme study / same categories and hierarchy</h4><div class="minitiles"><span>Code</span><span>Scratch</span><span>Cache</span></div></div></div><p>The installed Omarchy palette and font drive the app. Contrast, selection outlines, and labels remain readable when the theme changes. No continuous animation.</p></section><footer class="end">Choose a direction, or combine A's map with B's folder list.<br>These are static layout studies; the pictured controls do not operate on files.<nav class="nav"><a href="#atlas">Back to Atlas</a><a href="#navigator">Compare Navigator</a><a href="#reclaim">Compare Reclaim</a></nav></footer></main></body></html>'''
